// Merging two differently-typed *undeclared* function values in a choice is a
// genuinely heterogeneous merge (the result's return type is runtime-dependent)
// and must reject, never mis-type. The Int-returning and String-returning
// branches are not unifiable, so the unconstrained branch is rejected at its
// value read.
#use io

flag = 1 > 0
f = x => x + 1
g = y => "hi " + y
pick = flag | f | g
io::out $ pick(5)
